  "2026-11-12T23:05:13.631Z",codex-github230-1111,"Read-only real-data comparison: fresh public default-branch tracker copies, origin/main code be28728 versus the candidate, exact state-all atomic gated dry-run command with JSON, and complete public issue-only snapshots projected to read-only transport shapes. Counts create/update/unchanged: pm-github 8/16/0 versus 22/2/0; pm-review 0/4/0 versus 2/2/0; pm-rust 6/1/0 versus 6/1/0; pm-context 5/5/0 versus 7/3/0; pm-linear 3/6/0 versus 8/1/0. All candidate curated-content projections are unchanged. Four candidate gates pass. pm-github baseline refuses duplicate provenance references and the candidate refuses existing public source-body privacy findings; its counts are separately labeled production-planner diagnostics, not successful gated output. The literal no-extra-creates bound against released origin/main is not met because that release still binds reference-only items, the defect in issue 230. Supplemental native matcher comparison against the accepted pre-correction 4de7d4c shows creates 22,3,7,7,8 versus candidate 22,2,6,7,8, with no additional created issue in any repository. The three requested legacy examples resolve to their curated owner. Original tracker hashes were verified, no apply/commit/push was performed in copies, all scratch copies were deleted, and 25 GitHub API reads were used in total."
  "2026-11-12T23:09:19.319Z",codex-github230-1111,"Final self-review also corrected the inventory generator's prose migration: it now replaces both the original collector wording and the already-generated ownership paragraph, so the published inventory actually states unmarked leading legacy declaration compatibility. The existing three-case inventory file passes; reverting only that prose migration causes its round-trip contract assertion to fail, and restoration passes. Final lint and current typecheck pass after this change. The staged privacy audit passed across 9033 Git objects with approved identities and no secret or host-path findings. Releasing the renewed self-review claim; both PM issues remain open for orchestration."
  "2026-11-13T00:30:21.508Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 16 starts from clean b29cfb1; origin/main remains be28728 and is already merged. Read all seven named review threads in full, including every AI-agent prompt. Inventory index-builder callers and their scope; retain the complete peer index while refusing only in-scope targets, warning on unrelated conflicts. Validate every declared/importer number as a consistent positive safe integer; preserve legacy ownership and classify its actual declaration for repair planning. Add the reference-only webhook control, correct existing-owner docs, test native SDK must-refuse/must-allow cases and behavioral reverts, compare five read-only tracker previews with round 15, run bounded affected gates and both typechecks, then release the claim and honor the shared-runner hold before pushing. No review replies or resolutions."
  "2026-11-13T00:38:49.164Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 16 implementation: selected sync/export items and board-matched project candidates validate against the complete peer index; unrelated contradictory or duplicate owners emit structured warnings with both IDs. Import matching, persisted-plan receipts, refresh issue scopes and search-hit association now use their actual target scope. Native declarations must agree with their URL number and importer suffixes must be positive safe integers. Marker-free declarations remain repair owners; reference tags remain mentions. Native SDK regression matrix and webhook byte-preservation control added; focused verification and behavioural reverts underway."
  "2026-11-13T00:43:06.393Z",codex-github230-1111,"Gate follow-up: blockers coverage had an old expectation that clearing github_url also removed ownership despite retaining a valid leading GH issue declaration. The corrected legacy contract keeps that declaration authoritative. Added the declaration-only control and made the reference-only variant explicitly use middle-of-description prose; production blocker selection is unchanged. Current-sdk typecheck, test compilation, lint and docstring pass."
  "2026-11-13T00:46:01.466Z",codex-github230-1111,"Read-only public-data replay of round-15 tracker commits and complete issue snapshots, native CLI/SDK, exact state-all atomic gated preview: pm-github 22 create / 2 update / 0 unchanged; pm-review 2/2/0; pm-rust 6/1/0; pm-context 7/3/0; pm-linear 8/1/0. All counts identical to round 15, no new creates and zero curated-field changes; item/history bytes unchanged and scratch copies deleted. No new GitHub API reads were needed. The existing pm-github source-body privacy refusal remains; its counts come from the read-only production planner, not a successful gate. The other four native gates passed."
  "2026-11-13T01:03:06.802Z",codex-github230-1111,"The import-gate receipt fixture expected duplicate owners for issue 1 to refuse an import of issue 2, exactly the out-of-scope behavior this round removes. Corrected its must-refuse branch to target issue 1 and added a must-allow receipt for issue 2. The native SDK matrix independently covers the scoped import flow; the unchanged receipt checks still reject missing provenance and two entries targeting one item. No production adjustment was needed after this assertion."
  "2026-11-13T01:11:09.739Z",codex-github230-1111,"The packed consumer test hit its existing subprocess timeout while the broader gate was busy; its rerun is queued with the public-registry transport timer. The source-level mixed-import projection cases passed. Final ownership behavior preserves the accepted precedence of valid explicit/importer provenance over copied description markers, while malformed legacy number declarations yield no declaration claim and an invalid_github_identity_number warning. Scope and positive safe-integer fixes remain the only production behavior changes in this round."
