  "2026-11-13T01:45:49.086Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 16 final scope/data evidence: read all 7 requested threads, all 7 full comments and all 6 AI-agent prompts (Greptile has none). Selected IDs, board candidates and incoming targets validate against complete peers. Both IDs appear in off-scope collision warnings; a peer claiming an in-scope issue still refuses. Native declarations require their stated number to equal the URL number; unsafe importer suffixes and unsafe GitHub external_ref numbers establish no claim. Marker-free declarations remain repair owners, and reference-only webhook items remain byte-identical. The syntax-generated inventory documents every builder caller and its scope in docs/identity-ownership-inventory.md.\nRead-only public-data comparison replays the exact round-15 complete source snapshots against scratch clones pinned to the same public tracker commits; no apply and no new GitHub API reads. Round 15 -> round 16 create/update/unchanged: pm-github 22/2/0 -> 22/2/0; pm-review 2/2/0 -> 2/2/0; pm-rust 6/1/0 -> 6/1/0; pm-context 7/3/0 -> 7/3/0; pm-linear 8/1/0 -> 8/1/0. No extra creates and no curated-field changes. pm-github retains the known privacy preflight refusal on existing public issue bodies, so its counts are the read-only production planner diagnostic; the other four native gated previews pass. Native item/history hashes stayed identical and every scratch clone was deleted. No fleet checkout was written.\nOpen risks: CI must certify the capped import-gate remainder and full gates; two existing SDK compensation quarantines remain; the unchanged public-source privacy refusal remains visible. No new SDK gap or CLI defect was discovered. Claim will be released without closing; changelog regeneration and integrity checks follow the final tracker write."
  "2026-11-13T01:47:56.629Z",codex-github230-1111,"Final read-only checks: npm run changelog:full, npm run changelog:check and npm run privacy passed. The history remains a byte-prefix extension of b29cfb1; origin/main has no earlier record for this branch-created item. SDK verifyHistoryEntries verified all 233 current events with zero errors. Extra pm health --check-only --skip-vectors --strict-exit --summary reports native integrity OK, but exits 1 for the existing extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew (pinned 2026.11.6 versus host 2026.11.12) and also reports six stale in-progress items. Those are not part of the passing targeted gates and no version, telemetry or unrelated tracker data was changed. Claim is released; item remains in_progress and open."
  "2026-11-13T03:52:07.302Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 17: reproduce the unchanged 100 percent coverage gate first, then cover all missing behavior and fix the shared declaration diagnostics, deferred webhook deliveries and curated projection fixture. Read all six requested review threads including their agent prompts; behavioral reverts and the same five public snapshot previews will certify the fixes. Keep all thresholds, append-only history and current ownership guards."
  "2026-11-13T03:55:12.927Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 17 review receipt: five requested threads, five complete comments and four AI-agent prompts read (CodeQL has no agent prompt). This corrects the initial plan count. Baseline bun run coverage is running before source edits, with the original thresholds, real SDK storage and two workers. The diagnostic currently duplicates native declaration parsing, and webhook reconciliation currently acknowledges a delivery even when refresh deferred that issue."
  "2026-11-13T04:40:53.903Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 17 implementation: one shared native-declaration parser now supplies ownership and numeric diagnostics; the local URL regex and quadratic trim are removed. Quoted, bracketed and punctuated valid declarations agree with ownership, while real number mismatches warn. Refresh reports all deferred source issue numbers, and webhook reconciliation leaves their receipts pending while independent deliveries progress. The projection fixture now has explicit provenance and asserts one existing item plus literal tag preservation. Native Node 22 regressions and inventory CLI cases pass 26/26; full SDK reads ensure the performance fixture contains all 20,000 closing parentheses. The initial unfiltered bun coverage attempt reached its 45-minute cap before producing an aggregate report; no local coverage percentage is inferred from that timeout. Main 9a72437 was merged as a5f0273, with the changelog regenerated by the package command."
  "2026-11-13T04:40:54.889Z",codex-github230-1111,"Coverage-only simplification proof: native ownership snapshots use non-provisional claims. Their evidence flag implies at least one owner; owners are a subset of claims, and shared consistency refuses more than one claim. Therefore the later closeout evidence-without-one-owner check and its owners.length !== 1 disjunct cannot reject a native item. Refresh also receives at most one validated key, and every accepted collector produces a positive safe number, making the repeated cardinality and parsed-number checks unreachable. The raw github_number validation remains because malformed partial metadata can reach it. Real SDK controls verify unowned/same-repository closeout allowance, foreign/contradictory-owner refusal, invalid raw-number refusal, duplicate-record refusal, and valid refresh selection. No thresholds, source inventories or ignore rules changed."
  "2026-11-13T04:53:56.786Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 17 public read-only snapshot replay is complete: round-16 tracker commits and the same public source snapshots were replayed through the current packed build and native CLI/SDK. Create/update/unchanged counts remain pm-github 22/2/0, pm-review 2/2/0, pm-rust 6/1/0, pm-context 7/3/0 and pm-linear 8/1/0. No extra creates or curated-field changes. pm-github retains the existing public-source privacy preflight refusal, so its counts are the read-only production-planner diagnostic; the other four gated previews pass. No import was applied, source item/history hashes remain intact, zero new GitHub API reads were needed, and all scratch clones were deleted. Current typecheck, test-build typecheck, lint and the 33-module/315-declaration docstring gate pass; the minimum-SDK consumer remains queued behind the active two-worker coverage run."
  "2026-11-13T05:31:33.539Z",codex-github230-1111,"Additional coverage reachability proof: legacyGithubIdentityConflict is a retained compatibility API whose body always returns undefined, as required when gh: tags are mentions. Its former positive branches in import, sync and refresh can never execute for any item. Their scans and conditional emissions were removed, while empty typed receipt fields preserve the public optional identity_conflicts type and runtime absence. The shared explicit-ownership and peer checks still run. Minimum-SDK packed consumer validation passes 1/1 against 2026.10.23. The updated native regressions, inventory CLI and entire projection file pass 33/33. Focused instrumentation includes 87 test files and all 33 authored source modules with unchanged four-way 100 percent thresholds; slow suites remain for separate validation. No ignore rule or persistent gate configuration was changed."
  "2026-11-13T06:16:01.427Z",codex-github230-1111,"Coverage completion uses the native SDK and retained native V8 receipts at unchanged 100-percent thresholds for every authored module. Added behavioral outcomes for ownership index delegates and counters, missing dependency endpoints, malformed recovery targets, additive tags, outbound ownership drift, and exclusive recovery-plan publication. Eight targeted closeout revision/dependent-side-effect cases pass. The full baseline coverage command reached its 45-minute cap, so bounded source-complete test batches and the standard native receipt aggregator are used; no module exclusion or receipt URL filtering is introduced."
  "2026-11-13T06:24:43.669Z",codex-github230-1111,"Unreachable-branch proof: ownership index builders and updates always install a states entry together with byId and retain every claimant map, so fallback states/maps in private cache replacement cannot be absent. verifyImportIdempotency first selects a claim in the requested set, then the shared consistency check requires exactly one consistent unique owner; its later different-key/duplicate-owner branches cannot run. The atomic catch already rethrows both ownership codes before cleanup, making its second identical owner check unreachable. Plain citation matches always set linkOnly or preserveContent in prepareGithubImport and leave through that earlier branch, so the later mirroring branch cannot increment adopted. Removed only these redundant paths; typed shared refusals, reference-tag freedom and counters remain."
  "2026-11-13T06:27:13.998Z",codex-github230-1111,"Native SDK boundary observation: mutateItem permits a low-level callback to remove metadata.id, then listAllComplete correctly refuses that malformed document with list_source_incomplete. The disposable fixture now asserts that refusal and exercises the ownership cache missing-id boundary; no package behavior is weakened and no upstream SDK repair is included."
  "2026-11-13T06:29:42.608Z",codex-github230-1111,"Behavioral revert proof against 58ae396 in a disposable tracked-source copy, with finally restoration: reverting warnGithubOwnershipScope alone makes 6 of 9 boundary/diagnostic/20000-parenthesis regressions fail (valid controls remain); reverting runRefresh alone makes both deferred-number regressions fail; reverting reconcileGithubWebhooks alone makes the pending-delivery regression fail; removing only the curated fixture github_url seed makes both additive-provider-link cases fail because an extra item is created. Restored implementations pass 42/42 round-seventeen tests plus 2/2 fixture cases, with no setup exceptions or cancellations. Commands use timeout 1200 node --test --test-concurrency=1 and name patterns shared declaration boundaries/shared declaration diagnostics/native declaration diagnostics finish, deferred webhook/legacy retained refresh plans, deferred webhook, and additive provider links respectively."
  "2026-11-13T06:33:47.876Z",codex-github230-1111,"Read-only final-source public snapshot replay completed against the same round-16 tracker commits and source snapshots, with the exact scheduled --state all --atomic --gate --dry-run --json command and native installed package. Create/update/unchanged counts are identical: pm-github 22/2/0; pm-review 2/2/0; pm-rust 6/1/0; pm-context 7/3/0; pm-linear 8/1/0. No extra creates, no curated-field changes, all original tracker hashes unchanged, scratch clones removed, zero new GitHub issue API calls. pm-github preserves the already observed public-body privacy-preflight refusal; its identical counts are the read-only production-planner diagnostic, not a claimed passing gated command."
  "2026-11-13T06:57:20.579Z",codex-github230-1111,"Standalone import-gate.test.ts reached its required 20-minute cap after 70 passing cases and no assertion failures; three tail cases remain for a separate bounded command. Full closeout-revision.test.ts passes 110/110. The final source-complete coverage capture uses the current build, Node 22 for parent and children, two test workers, fresh native V8 receipts and the unchanged runCoverageGate source inventory/threshold validation. Current source and test typechecks, lint and the 33-file/315-declaration docstring gate pass."
